  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1200 AM CDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\nWednesday through Sunday:\n\nLooking at another surface low and associated mid-level \nshortwave trough to track across the region for Wednesday. \nAgain this system is trending to remain just far enough west \nand north from southern WI to limit moisture and precip chances \nfor Wednesday. Still looking at low-level WAA and above normal \ntemps for midweek as well. As the low pressure tracks across \nOntario to Hudson Bay Region Wednesday night into Thursday, the \nassociated cold front looks to drag across the Upper Midwest. \nWhile upper-level forcing looks to remain closer to the surface \nlow and upper-level trough to our north, mid-range models do \nprog moisture to increase in the warm sector. Pair the increased\nmoisture with PWATs above 1 inch and forcing along the cold \nfront, this looks to be our best chance to see some measurable \nrainfall across southern WI Thursday. Behind the front a cooler \nairmass will settle in toward the end of the week as high \npressure builds across the region through the weekend.\n\nWagner",
